  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-26T00:39:12.637Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There is a claim in the documentation that \"Manual synchronization is intended for data that changes infrequently and where intermediary values matter; like the positions of pieces on a chess board.\"\nHowever, if you try sending a new value (and calling RequestSerialization() ) each frame, you'll find that data is skipped - not every frame gets a serialization event. Docs should call out that RequestSerialization will cause variables to be captured at some point in the future, not necessarily on the same frame.",
